The solution has an error in enumeration. For p = 5 (p² = 25), the powers of 2 that can multiply are 2⁰, 2¹, 2², 2³, 2⁴, giving 25, 50, **100**, 200, 400. The value n = 100 = 2²·5² is missing; it satisfies r₂(100) = 4·3 = 12 and is < 500. Everything else checks out (m = 3 cases: 225, 450; p = 13: 169, 338; p = 17: 289).

Adding the missed value: 2146 + 100 = 2246.

